# RexMessages conventions

- Google DOM selectors live only in `src/preload/selectors.ts`. Never hard-code a Google selector anywhere else.
- `mainWorld()` in `src/preload/inject.ts` and `swMainWorld()` in `src/preload/sw.ts` are serialized by Electron. They must not reference imports or outer-scope variables.
- Preload entries (`inject`, `popup`, `gallery`, `sw`) are sandboxed CommonJS bundles. They must not import runtime code from each other (type-only imports from `src/shared/types.ts` are fine), or Rollup will emit a shared chunk that sandboxed preloads can't load.
- Quick reply must never send unless the open chat is confirmed as the sender's. Fail softly and tell the user.
- Google's page enforces Trusted Types: never use `innerHTML` in injected code.
- No Google-account automation (no scripted sign-in or credential handling).
- Keep `applyChromeIdentity()` in `src/main/index.ts` and the `window.chrome` members in `inject.ts`: without the "Google Chrome" client-hint brand, Google rejects sign-in as "This browser or app may not be secure". Never run the RexMessages hooks on `accounts.google.com`.
- Every `ipcMain` handler checks the sender (`isPageSender`, popup or gallery webContents) before acting.
- Electron 44 clipboard is async (`clipboard.write([new ClipboardItem(...)])`); `writeImage` no longer exists.
- After significant changes, update `README.md` and `CHANGELOG.md`.
